WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.267
Between harvests, exposed soil can dry quickly and wash or blow away. A cover crop puts leaves and roots where the ground would otherwise be bare.

00:00:09.267 --> 00:00:19.533
Leaves soften the impact of rain. Roots can make channels for water to enter the soil. When you end the cover crop, the remaining plant material can keep the soil shaded.

00:00:19.533 --> 00:00:30.133
Living plants also use water. Start on a small strip, count the water it takes to get the crop established, and plan to end it before it competes with your next crop.
